#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sech

#% text
# `sech(x)` gives the hyperbolic secant 1/cosh(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `sech(x)` stays unevaluated for symbolic `x`; where `cosh(x)` has an exact value, `sech(x)` is its reciprocal.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# `sech` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
sech(0)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
sech(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.6480542736638855

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Symbolic arguments and symmetry:

#% cell
sech(-x)
#% output
#= sech(x)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(sech(1), 30)
#% output
#= 0.6480542736638853995749773532261503

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `cosh`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan`
